Developer & Build Info
----------------------

Source and build instructions are maintained in the packaging repository:

    https://github.com/notolog/notolog-debian

The package installs a native PyInstaller one-file binary as /usr/bin/notolog.

Additional Notes
----------------

- `llama_cpp` and backend libraries are bundled and dynamically linked.
- Qt platform plugins may require `libxcb-cursor0` or related dependencies.
- Check the system's PIE/hardening status with `hardening-check /usr/bin/notolog`

Support & Feedback
------------------

To report packaging issues, visit:

    https://github.com/notolog/notolog-debian/issues

For application bugs or feature requests:

    https://github.com/notolog/notolog-editor/issues

Text-to-Speech
--------------

PCM audio playback uses the system PortAudio library. Install NeMo-Speech.cpp 0.2.0
separately, select its nemo-speech executable in Text-to-Speech settings, and download
the models from those settings. Neither the runtime nor the models is included in
this package. Model downloads use the user's data directory by default and do not
require administrator privileges.
The speech worker keeps document text and generated audio in memory.
